      "note": "Promotes 'positive reference controls remain detectable by the public npm surface' out of redact-secret-benchmarks' regressions.test.mjs (benchmarks issue #16). The negative direction (reference/pointer syntax excluded) is already canonical via issues #292 and #293; this record supplies the missing positive direction -- that generic-token's reference-syntax exclusions do not also swallow literal credentials. The two canonical fixtures sit on the issue #292 boundary directly (is_env_var_identifier in generic_token.rs): a %...%- or :-delimited value whose interior contains '-' is not a bare identifier, so it fails the Windows-env/SQL-bind reference grammar and stays detected. Both were confirmed to already pass against the current detector before being added, so this closes an uncovered contract rather than a live regression; gates stay pending until supported-surface evidence and a fixed-candidate benchmark rerun are recorded. No benchmark fixture input or discovery-matrix material was copied -- both canonical inputs are freshly constructed synthetic values."
